  "summary": "Malicious code in phonoviatts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (4942401da983144b311dfb23a91c860e43764e88b8c8975dacdb349e9b637b5e)\nAnalysis of phonoviatts 0.1.0 surfaced no indicators of installer-side harm: no install-time or import-time network activity, no credential or environment scraping, no execution of fetched content, no persistence mechanism, and no silent relay of caller-supplied data to a non-first-party destination.\n\n## Source: kam193 (0ad248ff66471a497d4c3a6d16384648636101a927c384cd4870adf920eced97)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
